{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789333115,"nonce":"5EpAB+phP9HPYh3fny5JJdRdRoU=","title":"ZynML: a lambda capturing a local panics in Cranelift lowering","message":"def main() -\u003e i64 {\n        let k: i64 = 3\n        let step: (i64, i64) =\u003e i64 = def(acc, i): acc + (i + k) % 8\n        let mut total: i64 = 0\n        let mut i: i64 = 0\n        while i \u003c 10 {\n            total = step(total, i)\n            i = i + 1\n        }\n        return total\n    }\n\npanics with \"Binary op left operand HirId not in value_map\" in the\nCranelift backend. Without the capture (`acc + i % 8`) the same program\ncompiles and runs. `crates/zynml/benchmarks/bench_lambda_call.zynml` uses\nthe capture-free form for this reason, and there is no ZynML counterpart\nto `bench_closure_call.py` until this is fixed.\n\nNot yet run on the other backends.","files":null}]}